Ticket #4471 is not one date bug. Its 412 unique reports split into two causes when grouped
by the tenant's date locale, booking form, and intake channel.

## The two causes

### Shared parser reads day-first dates as month-first — 379 reports

For these reports, the tenant writes day before month but the shared parser reads month first.
The date therefore lands on a different day. These reports span 11 tenants and arrived through
the app, email, and booking forms.

### booking-v3 gives day-first users a month-first hint — 33 reports

These reports came from booking-v3 forms. The form tells people to enter `MM/DD/YYYY`, while
the tenant's locale reads dates day first. The hint and the tenant's date interpretation
disagree, so this is a separate cause from the shared parser.

<Callout>
The intake tag is only a guess, not the cause. Classify by tenant, form, and channel: 23
parser reports were tagged hint, and 15 hint reports were tagged parser.
</Callout>

## Reports merged into #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The export contains 427 rows but only 412 report IDs; the 15 repeated rows are overlapping
export pages, not additional reports. The five desk notes that describe a one-day move all
remain in the parser group under the tenant-and-channel rule. They are not a third cause in
this export.

